IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-licensee-duties`

-- g3-tests-licensee-duties.l4: tests of sections 12 to 16, written by ENCODER G3.
--
-- Every expected value was decided from the Hebrew text of the Law (inputs/law.wiki lines 129-142, checked against the gazette
-- page 185) and from Interpretation Law s.10 BEFORE the module was run.  The dates were counted with an independent calendar
-- script (python datetime), not with the module.  The calendars of rest days are ILLUSTRATIONS: no holiday is computed, and
-- nothing here states the calendar of any year.  The wordings of Israeli Standard 994 are ILLUSTRATIONS too: the Standard is not
-- in the sources, only the fact that each wording carries the day it took effect and the findings on the work.
--
-- Lines of the form `-- TRACE-EXPECT: ...` above a #TRACE state what the trace must print; check-traces.py reads them,
-- because a DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT.

§ `Tests of sections 12 to 16`

§§ `Fixtures`

`fixture — Amit, an individual` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "IL-100", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`fixture — Bar, an individual` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "IL-200", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
-- The same reference as Amit under another description: identity is the reference, not the whole record.
`fixture — Amit again, described as a corporation` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "IL-100", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

`fixture — the licence held by Amit` MEANS Licence WITH
    `the holder` IS `fixture — Amit, an individual`
    `the kind of licence` IS `grade 2 licence`
    `a temporary licence under section 9` IS FALSE
    `granted on` IS YMD 2026 2 1
    `renewed on` IS EMPTY
    `validity ends on, as recorded` IS NOTHING
    `revoked on` IS NOTHING
    `suspended from` IS NOTHING
    `suspended until` IS NOTHING

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` MEANS LIST `grade 2 licence`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Licence kind`
`fixture — no licence is in force` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — no day is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2026 3 31

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — 31 March and 1 April 2026 are days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2026 3 31, YMD 2026 4 1

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — 15 March 2026 is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2026 3 15

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`fixture — 1 April 2026 is a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2026 4 1

§§ `12. A licence is personal`

-- Text: "a licensee shall not transfer the licence in his hand to another person and shall not permit another person to use his licence".
-- Both limbs bind a licensee, once the Law has commenced; "another person" is a person other than the holder (identity by reference).
#ASSERT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Bar, an individual` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Amit, an individual` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Amit again, described as a corporation` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.12 — permitting the person to use the licence breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Bar, an individual` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — permitting the person to use the licence breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Amit, an individual` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- The prohibition binds a licensee: with no licence in force the holder is not one.
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Bar, an individual` `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — permitting the person to use the licence breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Bar, an individual` `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE
-- Before commencement for the work there is no duty (fork COM: the input is read as "the Law has commenced for the licensee's work").
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — a transfer of the licence to the person breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Bar, an individual` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s.12 — permitting the person to use the licence breaches section 12` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` `fixture — Bar, an individual` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` FALSE

-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.12: the licensee transferred the licence to another person
#TRACE `s.12 — the licensee shall not transfer the licence or permit another person to use it` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `transfer the licence to another person` `fixture — Bar, an individual` AT 3
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.12: the licensee permitted another person to use the licence
#TRACE `s.12 — the licensee shall not transfer the licence or permit another person to use it` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `permit another person to use the licence` `fixture — Bar, an individual` AT 3
-- A transfer to the holder himself is not a transfer to another person: the prohibitions stand, unbreached.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | transfer the licence to another person
#TRACE `s.12 — the licensee shall not transfer the licence or permit another person to use it` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `transfer the licence to another person` `fixture — Amit, an individual` AT 3
-- No sunset: a year later, nothing done, the prohibitions still stand (a SHANT with a WITHIN would have lapsed).
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | permit another person to use the licence
#TRACE `s.12 — the licensee shall not transfer the licence or permit another person to use it` `fixture — the licence held by Amit` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `13. The Standard and the work`

-- Three illustrative wordings of Israeli Standard 994.  The first took effect on 1 January 2020 and the work conformed to all of it.
-- The second took effect on 1 January 2026 and added a requirement of part 5 that the work did not meet.
-- The third is a wording under which the tightness test of the testing chapter of part 4 was not performed.
-- Fields in order: day took effect; part 4; tightness test; part 5.
GIVETH A `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`fixture — wording of 2020, all conformed` MEANS `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
    `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2020 1 1
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS TRUE
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS TRUE
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met` MEANS `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
    `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS TRUE
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS TRUE
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test` MEANS `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
    `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2020 1 1
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS FALSE
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS FALSE
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS TRUE

-- Part 4 not met for another reason than the tightness test: the test was performed.
GIVETH A `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`fixture — wording of 2020, part 4 not met but the tightness test performed` MEANS `Wording of Israeli Standard 994` WITH
    `the day this wording took effect` IS YMD 2020 1 1
    `the work conformed to part 4 of this wording` IS FALSE
    `a tightness test of the refrigerant piping was performed as the testing chapter of part 4 of this wording requires` IS TRUE
    `the work conformed to part 5 of this wording` IS TRUE

GIVETH A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` MEANS LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, all conformed`, `fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Wording of Israeli Standard 994`
`fixture — the wordings of 2026 and 2020, in the other order` MEANS LIST `fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`, `fixture — wording of 2020, all conformed`

GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`fixture — a system of 25 kilowatts` MEANS `Cooling system` WITH
    `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 25
    `refrigerants` IS EMPTY

-- Installation by Amit on 31 December 2025, the last day before the 2026 wording; on 1 January 2026, its first day; on 10 March 2026.
GIVETH A `Work item`
`fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS `fixture — Amit, an individual`
    `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
    `the system` IS `fixture — a system of 25 kilowatts`
    `date performed` IS YMD 2025 12 31

GIVETH A `Work item`
`fixture — installation on 1 January 2026` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS `fixture — Amit, an individual`
    `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
    `the system` IS `fixture — a system of 25 kilowatts`
    `date performed` IS YMD 2026 1 1

GIVETH A `Work item`
`fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS `fixture — Amit, an individual`
    `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
    `the system` IS `fixture — a system of 25 kilowatts`
    `date performed` IS YMD 2026 3 10

GIVETH A `Work item`
`fixture — maintenance on 10 March 2026` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS `fixture — Amit, an individual`
    `the kind of job` IS `a maintenance job`
    `the system` IS `fixture — a system of 25 kilowatts`
    `date performed` IS YMD 2026 3 10

GIVETH A `Work item`
`fixture — installation on 31 December 2019` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS `fixture — Amit, an individual`
    `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
    `the system` IS `fixture — a system of 25 kilowatts`
    `date performed` IS YMD 2019 12 31

-- The wording is the one in force on the day of the work ("as their wording is from time to time"): the latest wording that took effect
-- on or before that day, the day it took effect being inside.
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 1 January 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- The order in which the wordings are supplied changes nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` `fixture — the wordings of 2026 and 2020, in the other order` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 1 January 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2026 and 2020, in the other order` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- Alternative S13a: judged against the wording in force on the day of the inspection (1 June 2026), the work of 31 December 2025 breaches section 13.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13, judged against the wording in force on the day of the inspection` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` (YMD 2026 6 1) `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- Judged against the wording of the day of the inspection when that is still the old wording: no breach.
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13, judged against the wording in force on the day of the inspection` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` (YMD 2025 12 31) `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- No wording in force on the day of the work: the sources do not answer, so the answer is a named refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2019` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE BECAUSE "s.13: no wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on the day the work is judged against was supplied, so conformity to parts 4 and 5 cannot be answered"
-- A work that section 13 does not reach is not refused: the limbs that decide are read first.
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2019` EMPTY TRUE `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` FALSE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE
-- Maintenance is work too (part 5 of the Standard): the wording of 2026 is not met by the maintenance of 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — maintenance on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE

-- Third Schedule item (4) prices ONE failure under s.13: an installation without the tightness test of the testing chapter of part 4.
-- The listed violation is JUST that item when section 13 applies, the job is an installation and the test was not performed
-- under the wording in force on the day; in every other case NOTHING, which says "no Third Schedule row", not "no breach" (T13).
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS JUST `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- Maintenance without the test: a breach of section 13, but item (4) speaks of an installation only.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — maintenance on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — maintenance on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Installation conforming to every part: no breach and no listed violation.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, all conformed`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Installation with part 4 not met for another reason, the test performed: a breach of section 13 with no Third Schedule row.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the licensee breached section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, part 4 not met but the tightness test performed`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, part 4 not met but the tightness test performed`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Installation with part 5 not met only (the 2026 wording): a breach, no listed violation.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The tightness test is read against the wording in force on the day of the work too: before the 2026 wording the 2020 wording governs.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`, `fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS JUST `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`, `fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 13 binds a licensee only: an unlicensed installer without the test is caught by s.3(a), not here.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`) TRUE `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Alternative S13c: item (4) frozen to the wording in force on a fixed day.  On 10 March 2026 the wording of 2026 is in force and the test was performed under it
-- (NOTHING, as above); frozen to 14 January 2025 the 2020 wording, under which no test was performed, is the one, so the item is committed.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13, the testing chapter being that of the wording in force on a fixed day` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (YMD 2025 1 14) (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`, `fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS JUST `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
#ASSERT `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13, the testing chapter being that of the wording in force on a fixed day` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (YMD 2026 3 10) (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`, `fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A fixed day before every wording: no answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s.13 — the listed violation committed under section 13, the testing chapter being that of the wording in force on a fixed day` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` (YMD 2019 1 1) (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`, `fixture — wording of 2026, part 5 not met`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE BECAUSE "s.13: no wording of Israeli Standard 994 in force on the day the work is judged against was supplied, so conformity to parts 4 and 5 cannot be answered"

-- The record Chapter 6 takes: violator, listed violation, reference for the act, day of the act.
#ASSERT `s.13 — the violation committed under section 13` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` "act-13-1" (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Violation WITH `the violator` IS `fixture — Amit, an individual`, `the listed violation` IS `installation without the tightness test of the piping`, `reference for the act` IS "act-13-1", `date of the act` IS YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `s.13 — the violation committed under section 13` `fixture — maintenance on 10 March 2026` "act-13-2" (LIST `fixture — wording of 2020, no tightness test`) TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The prohibition of work not in accordance with the Standard, as a rule: the non-conforming work is the breach, the conforming work leaves it standing.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.13: the work was not done in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994
#TRACE `s.13 — the licensee shall do the work in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `perform work on a cooling system` AT 5
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | perform work on a cooling system
#TRACE `s.13 — the licensee shall do the work in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `perform work on a cooling system` AT 5

-- Alternative S13b: the same facts under the text's own form, a MUST with no deadline.  The conforming work discharges it; the non-conforming work does not match the
-- act, so the duty merely stands and no breach can be traced however long the clock runs: which is why the reading taken is a prohibition.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.13 — the licensee must perform the work in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994, in the text's own form` `fixture — installation on 31 December 2025` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `perform work on a cooling system` AT 5
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | perform work on a cooling system
#TRACE `s.13 — the licensee must perform the work in accordance with parts 4 and 5 of Israeli Standard 994, in the text's own form` `fixture — installation on 10 March 2026` `fixture — the wordings of 2020 and 2026` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `perform work on a cooling system` AT 5
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `14. Showing the licence`

GIVETH A `Demand to see the licence`
`fixture — the orderer demanded and was refused` MEANS `Demand to see the licence` WITH
    `the person demanding ordered the work` IS TRUE
    `the person demanded to see the licence` IS TRUE
    `the licensee failed to show the licence on the demand` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Demand to see the licence`
`fixture — the orderer demanded and the licensee showed the licence` MEANS `Demand to see the licence` WITH
    `the person demanding ordered the work` IS TRUE
    `the person demanded to see the licence` IS TRUE
    `the licensee failed to show the licence on the demand` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Demand to see the licence`
`fixture — the orderer did not demand` MEANS `Demand to see the licence` WITH
    `the person demanding ordered the work` IS TRUE
    `the person demanded to see the licence` IS FALSE
    `the licensee failed to show the licence on the demand` IS FALSE

-- A person who did not order the work asks to see the licence: section 14 gives him nothing.
GIVETH A `Demand to see the licence`
`fixture — a stranger demanded and was refused` MEANS `Demand to see the licence` WITH
    `the person demanding ordered the work` IS FALSE
    `the person demanded to see the licence` IS TRUE
    `the licensee failed to show the licence on the demand` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` `fixture — the orderer demanded and was refused` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` `fixture — the orderer demanded and was refused` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` `fixture — the orderer demanded and the licensee showed the licence` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` `fixture — the orderer demanded and the licensee showed the licence` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- No demand, no duty: nothing is owed before the orderer asks.
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` `fixture — the orderer did not demand` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` `fixture — the orderer did not demand` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- Only the orderer of the work may demand.
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` `fixture — a stranger demanded and was refused` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee breached section 14` `fixture — a stranger demanded and was refused` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- The work must be work on a cooling system; the person a licensee; the Law commenced.
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` `fixture — the orderer demanded and was refused` FALSE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` `fixture — the orderer demanded and was refused` TRUE `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.14 — the licensee must show the licence` `fixture — the orderer demanded and was refused` TRUE `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` FALSE

-- The orderer's demand is a liberty (MAY); once made, the licensee's duty stands until he shows the licence (no time is stated).
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | show the licence to the orderer of the work
#TRACE `s.14 — the orderer of the work may demand to see the licence, and the licensee must then show it` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the orderer of the work` DOES `demand to see the licence` AT 0
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.14 — the orderer of the work may demand to see the licence, and the licensee must then show it` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the orderer of the work` DOES `demand to see the licence` AT 0
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `show the licence to the orderer of the work` AT 2
-- Never demanded: the permission stands, nothing is owed.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | demand to see the licence
#TRACE `s.14 — the orderer of the work may demand to see the licence, and the licensee must then show it` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `15. The Registrar's demand for reports, information and documents`

-- A demand is of one of two kinds, each with its own limit: a report must concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee;
-- information or documents must be needed, in the Registrar's opinion, to realise the purposes of the Law.
-- Fields in order: kind; particulars concern the engagement; opinion that they are needed; made as a condition of renewal or extension;
-- day of the demand; the day directed for compliance.
GIVETH A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
`fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` MEANS `Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH
    `the kind of demand` IS `a report on particulars of the licensee's engagement as a licensee`
    `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS FALSE
    `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 15)

-- A report demand whose particulars do NOT concern the engagement, though the Registrar thinks them needed: the limbs are distinct.
GIVETH A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
`fixture — a report not on the engagement but thought needed` MEANS `Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH
    `the kind of demand` IS `a report on particulars of the licensee's engagement as a licensee`
    `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS FALSE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS TRUE
    `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 15)

GIVETH A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
`fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` MEANS `Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH
    `the kind of demand` IS `information or documents needed to realise the purposes of the Law`
    `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS FALSE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS TRUE
    `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS TRUE
    `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS NOTHING

-- Documents NOT thought needed, though the particulars concern the engagement: the other limb does not help.
GIVETH A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
`fixture — documents not thought needed but concerning the engagement` MEANS `Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH
    `the kind of demand` IS `information or documents needed to realise the purposes of the Law`
    `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS FALSE
    `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 15)

GIVETH A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
`fixture — a report directed for the day of the demand` MEANS `Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH
    `the kind of demand` IS `a report on particulars of the licensee's engagement as a licensee`
    `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS FALSE
    `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)

GIVETH A `Demand of the Registrar under section 15`
`fixture — a report directed for a day before the demand` MEANS `Demand of the Registrar under section 15` WITH
    `the kind of demand` IS `a report on particulars of the licensee's engagement as a licensee`
    `the particulars concern the licensee's engagement as a licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or documents are needed to realise the purposes of the Law` IS FALSE
    `the demand is made as a condition for renewing or extending the licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the demand` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `the day the Registrar directed that the report or supply be made by` IS JUST (YMD 2026 2 28)

#ASSERT `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` `fixture — a report not on the engagement but thought needed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` `fixture — documents not thought needed but concerning the engagement` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- The power is over a licensee, once the Law has commenced.
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the Registrar has the power to make the demand` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` FALSE

-- "As he directed": the days from the demand to the day directed, the day of the demand not counted (IL s.10(a)): 1 March to 15 March is 14 days.
#ASSERT `s.15 — the days from the demand within which the licensee must comply` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `s.15 — the days from the demand within which the licensee must comply` `fixture — a report directed for the day of the demand` EQUALS JUST 0
-- No day directed: the text states no limit, so there is none.
#ASSERT `s.15 — the days from the demand within which the licensee must comply` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A day directed before the demand cannot be counted to: named refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s.15 — the days from the demand within which the licensee must comply` `fixture — a report directed for a day before the demand` BECAUSE "s.15: the day the Registrar directed for compliance precedes the day of the demand, so no period can be counted"

-- The licensee's duty to comply (fork S15b): taken, it follows the power for both limbs; the alternative reads the last clause of s.15 as reaching only information or documents.
#ASSERT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand` `fixture — a report not on the engagement but thought needed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand, the express duty reaching only information or documents` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand, the express duty reaching only information or documents` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the licensee must comply with the demand, the express duty reaching only information or documents` `fixture — documents not thought needed but concerning the engagement` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE

-- The condition for renewal or extension: a demand made on that footing is satisfied only by supply.
#ASSERT NOT `s.15 — the condition for renewing or extending the licence is satisfied` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` FALSE
#ASSERT `s.15 — the condition for renewing or extending the licence is satisfied` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.15 — the condition for renewing or extending the licence is satisfied` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT `s.15 — the condition for renewing or extending the licence is satisfied` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` TRUE

-- The demand, then the licensee's duty.  The licensee's clock runs from the demand: 14 days, the day directed being inside.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.15 — the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents, and the licensee must supply them` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to report, or to supply information or documents` AT 0
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `report, or supply the information or documents, that the Registrar required` AT 14
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.15: the licensee did not report or supply what the Registrar demanded
#TRACE `s.15 — the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents, and the licensee must supply them` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to report, or to supply information or documents` AT 0
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `report, or supply the information or documents, that the Registrar required` AT 15
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.15: the licensee did not report or supply what the Registrar demanded
#TRACE `s.15 — the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents, and the licensee must supply them` `fixture — a report on the engagement, directed for 15 March 2026` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to report, or to supply information or documents` AT 0
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 15)
-- No day directed: no deadline, so the licensee's duty stands however long it takes, and supply at any time discharges it.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.15 — the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents, and the licensee must supply them` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to report, or to supply information or documents` AT 0
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `report, or supply the information or documents, that the Registrar required` AT 400
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | report, or supply the information or documents, that the Registrar required
#TRACE `s.15 — the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents, and the licensee must supply them` `fixture — documents thought needed, no day directed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require the licensee to report, or to supply information or documents` AT 0
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- A demand the Registrar has no power to make: the rule owes nothing.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.15 — the Registrar may demand a report, information or documents, and the licensee must supply them` `fixture — a report not on the engagement but thought needed` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `16. Notice of a change in the application particulars`

-- Fields in order of the fixture constructor: the particular was one given in the application; the day of the change; the Registrar
-- directed a manner; the notice followed it; the day the notice was given.
GIVEN `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given to the Registrar` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Change in the application particulars`
`fixture — a change` `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application` `the day of the change` `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying` `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed` `the day the notice was given to the Registrar` MEANS
    `Change in the application particulars` WITH
        `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application` IS `the particular was one the licensee gave in a licence application`
        `the day of the change` IS `the day of the change`
        `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying` IS `the Registrar directed a manner of notifying`
        `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed` IS `the notice followed the manner the Registrar directed`
        `the day the notice was given to the Registrar` IS `the day the notice was given to the Registrar`

-- The last day: 30 days from the day of the change, the day of the change not counted (IL s.10(a)), then IL s.10(c).
-- 1 March 2026 + 30 days = 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
-- 31 March a day of rest: the last day moves to 1 April.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1
-- 31 March and 1 April both days of rest: 2 April (the reading of the time module, its fork F3).
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — 31 March and 1 April 2026 are days of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 4 2
-- A day of rest in the middle of the period is counted as a day of it and moves nothing.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — 15 March 2026 is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
-- A day of rest just AFTER the nominal last day moves nothing either.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — 1 April 2026 is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
-- Month ends and a leap year: 31 January 2026 + 30 days = 2 March 2026; 1 February 2028 + 30 days = 2 March 2028; 15 December 2026 + 30 days = 14 January 2027.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 1 31) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2028 2 1) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2028 3 2
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar of a change made on` (YMD 2026 12 15) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 14
-- The alternative (fork S16, kind D): without IL s.10(c) the last day is the thirtieth day even if it is a day of rest.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the last day for notifying the Registrar, counting only IL s.10(a), of a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
-- The days the licensee has, the WITHIN of the rule: 30, 31, 32.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the number of days allowed for notifying a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s.16 — the number of days allowed for notifying a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `s.16 — the number of days allowed for notifying a change made on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `fixture — 31 March and 1 April 2026 are days of rest` EQUALS 32

-- Notice in time: on the last day it is in time, on the next day it is late.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 31))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`
-- The day of the change itself is inside (the notice may come at once).
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`
-- With 31 March a day of rest, 1 April is in time and 2 April is late.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1))) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 4 2))) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest`
-- No notice given is not notice in time.
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`
-- A particular that the licensee did not give in the application is outside section 16.
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`
-- A manner directed by the Registrar and followed counts; directed and not followed does not; not directed, the flag is irrelevant.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee gave notice of the change in time` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest`

-- Breach as at a day: a missing notice is not a breach until the last day has passed.
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 3 31) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 4 1) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 4 1) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 4 2) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- A late notice is a breach whenever it is looked at after it was given; a timely one never is.
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 6 1) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 6 1) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 31))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- A notice not in the manner directed is no notice: as at the last day not yet a breach, the day after it is.
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 3 31) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 4 1) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE
-- Outside section 16: not a licensee, the Law not commenced, a particular not given in the application.
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 6 1) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 6 1) (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s.16 — the licensee breached section 16 as at` (YMD 2026 6 1) (`fixture — a change` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE

-- The duty as a rule.  The clock starts at 0 on the day of the change; WITHIN is 30, or more when IL s.10(c) moves the last day.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` AT 30
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.16: the licensee did not notify the Registrar of the change in the particulars given in the licence application within 30 days
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` AT 31
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.16: the licensee did not notify the Registrar of the change in the particulars given in the licence application within 30 days
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)
-- On the last day itself the duty still stands, with no day left.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING | WITHIN 0
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)
-- With 31 March a day of rest the licensee has 31 days: day 31 is in time and day 32 is not.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` AT 31
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.16: the licensee did not notify
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — 31 March 2026 is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` AT 32
-- A notice not in the manner the Registrar directed does not match the act: the duty runs on and is breached.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACHED | s.16: the licensee did not notify
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — a grade 2 licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the licensee` DOES `notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` AT 10
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)
-- Not a licensee: the rule owes nothing.
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s.16 — the licensee must notify the Registrar of a change in the application particulars` (`fixture — a change` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) `fixture — no day is a day of rest` `fixture — no licence is in force` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
